data: {"id":"chatcmpl-efe77d06-bdbf-466f-9a3c-ec43b8275778","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795552645,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"`AbstractList` with `RandomAccess` appears highly efficient for returning transaction IDs, avoiding significant overhead by boxing `Long` objects only when accessed.  Ensure `get(int index)` includes `IndexOutOfBoundsException` checks.  Analyzing `Persistent AVL Tree` node size on a 64-bit JVM, the memory overhead seems manageable.\n\n#### Case 3: Persistent AVL Tree (`StateNode`) vs Mutable State when `openCount == 0`?\nThe node size of `Persistent AVL Tree` (`StateNode`) is being analyzed on a 64-bit JVM, assessing if the memory footprint is manageable for `StateNode`. The key aspect is comparing its overhead with mutable state when the open transaction count is zero. Considering the node structure's size is essential to ensure efficient garbage collection.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

