data: {"id":"chatcmpl-efe77d06-bdbf-466f-9a3c-ec43b8275778","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795552645,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"The `putSeq` method for inserting sequence numbers into the AVL tree is validated, confirming efficient balancing and correct updating of node metadata. If the key exists, the sequence number is updated, leveraging the non-decreasing nature of commit sequence numbers to potentially avoid node creation. The `getSeq` method performs point queries to retrieve sequence numbers, efficiently returning the sequence number or a default value (0) if the key is not found, with an optional check to prune the tree traversal if a maximum sequence number is less than or equal to a threshold. Further optimization is possible in the conflict check by checking if `n.maxSeq <= threshold` which is faster than calling `compareTo`.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

data: {"id":"chatcmpl-efe77d06-bdbf-466f-9a3c-ec43b8275778","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795552645,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"If no writes have happened since the transaction began, conflict detection can be skipped entirely, requiring only a single check. Specifically, if `currentCommitSeq == tx.beginCommitSeq`, the transaction cannot conflict, thus eliminating the need for `tx.readSet` and `tx.readRanges` iteration. This optimization streamlines conflict detection in the common \"no-write\" scenario by skipping the need for a full read set/range scan.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

data: {"id":"chatcmpl-efe77d06-bdbf-466f-9a3c-ec43b8275778","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795552645,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"Conflict detection optimization targets efficiency by reducing unnecessary iterations. A `hasRangeSeqGreater` helper function, utilizing optional bounds (lo, hi), efficiently checks for conflicting sequence numbers within a specified key range without iterating when `n == null || n.maxSeq <= threshold`. The `hasRangeSeqGreater` function's logic is meticulously designed to optimize the search process within the AVL tree. The goal is to perform an efficient check by leveraging the structure of the AVL tree to determine if a conflict exists.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

